  "caption": "Quinn's knee started creaking on the stairs, so Quinn retired to the floor. The knee got stiffer.\n\nWith knee arthritis, exercise is a first-line treatment, not something to avoid. How a knee looks on an X-ray often says little about how it feels, and cartilage tends to respond well to sensible, gradual load.\n\nWhat often helps: strength work as the centrepiece (sit-to-stands, step-ups, gradual squats, about twice a week), low-impact cardio like cycling, water walking or brisk walking, and accepting a mild ache that settles within a day. After a flare, dial back rather than stop. Sleep, pacing and a healthy weight can help too.\n\nSharp pain, swelling or night pain are signs to ease off and get reassessed.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
